ts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test2/diagnostic-match: Match compiler diagnostic code, span, profile, target and remediation with stable tool-usable output. Concrete acceptance: Change code, source span, category, profile, target or remediation independently; fail mismatches even if localized message text differs legitimately. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test2/generated-reentry: Execute generated-code test fixtures through the normal compiler pipeline and assert retained source/generated provenance. Concrete acceptance: Submit generated source that is well shaped but type/effect/profile/capability/safety illegal or lacks producer origins; normal pipeline validation must reject before downstream execution. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test2/optimization-soundness: Reject unsound compiler rewrites and remove safety checks only with evidence that preserves safe semantics. Concrete acceptance: Execute an unsound rewrite and proofless safety-check deletion alongside the valid rewrite; fail preservation and prevent a claimed optimization pass. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test2/plugin-boundaries: Exercise compiler plugin capability, profile and pass-boundary enforcement without ambient authority. Concrete acceptance: Try an ungranted plugin effect, a write outside its pass boundary, incompatible profile or undeclared transformed fact; the fixture must observe denial before