 report and any safe-package release claim consuming it. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test5/runtime-checks: Demonstrate both passing and deterministic failing runtime-check paths for valid and invalid inputs. Concrete acceptance: For each supported check execute valid and invalid inputs; require normal success and deterministic declared failure with source identity, never undefined host behavior. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test5/safe-outcomes: Exercise each safety mechanism with positive, negative and unsafe-audited fixtures; safe code must never depend on undefined behavior and negative cases reject with stable diagnostics under the four declared safety outcomes. Concrete acceptance: For every claimed safety mechanism execute positive, negative and audited-unsafe fixtures; reject absent/fifth outcomes, safe-code undefined behavior and unstable negative diagnostics. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test5/taint: Trace source, validation and sink and reject unvalidated taint sinks, including bypass attempts. Concrete acceptance: Follow tainted source through validation to the actual sink, then bypass the validator or substitute unrelated validation; deny the sink and fail a trace that hides the bypass. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test5/unsafe-audit: Inspect actual unsafe-fixture audit artifacts and fail or reject unaudited unsafe fixture results. Concrete acceptance: Inspect the emitted audit records from actual unsafe fixture execution; remove owner/reason/review/source/evidence or the audit entirely and fail the fixture rather than emitting a generic audit-shaped report. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. This producer supplies conformance evidence; independent intermediate admission and final release remain separate consumers. Current implementation acceptance is unassessed.",
