   "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-staged-compiler-validation` Execute staged compiler validation\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [TEST13](../../docs/phase-14-testing-verification-and-conformance/202-test13-self-hosting-validation-plan.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Implement and execute the Execute staged compiler validation runner against actual declared owner interfaces, retaining the exact implementation/compiler/source/fixture/profile/target and applicable runtime/backend/provider identities. Run the named passing and failing cases; missing evidence is failure for the claimed scope, while inapplicable cases are explicitly reported. Source bootstrap/release-supply-chain: Require the active release policy's provenance, SBOM, signatures and reproducibility evidence on bootstrap release candidates. Concrete acceptance: Under the active release policy remove required provenance, SBOM, signature or reproducibility evidence, tamper the candidate identity, or revoke an input; reject the claim. Preserve TEST13 signed-or-otherwise-verifiable provenance: signing is mandatory only when that policy requires it. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source bootstrap/trust-reduction: Make the trusted compiler-source boundary and its change across a migration explicit and measurable. Concrete acceptance: Claim a reduced trusted base with no exact before/after compiler-source and host/toolchain inventory or with unchanged trust merely because source moved to Gravity; fail the claim and retain residual host dependencies. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test13/diagnostic-schema: Preserve self-hosted compiler diagnostic source spans/stable codes and artifact schemas. Concrete acceptance: Compile accepted and rejected fixtures with both named stages and compare stable codes, source spans and artifact schemas; fail lost origins or incompatible unexplained schemas. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test13/rebuild-equivalence: Rebuild staged compilers with source/compiler/lockfile/target-matrix/output hashes; classify expected/unexpected output differences and reject unexplained divergence. Concrete acceptance: Actually rebuild each claimed next stage from pinned source/compiler/lockfile/target inputs and compare outputs; fail unexplained divergence or supplied output records with no executed rebuild. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test13/report: Emit stage manifest/compiler artifact, conformance report, rebuild log, stage comparison report, provenance attestation, TCB delta and unsafe audit report. Concrete acceptance: Remove stage manifest/compiler artifact/conformance/rebuild/comparison/provenance/TCB/audit links required by the stage; reject missing or unrelated evidence and retain explicit implemented-subset limits. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test13/stage-conformance: Run conformance suites required for the stage's implemented subset; deny stage advancement without those passes. Concrete acceptance: Invoke the applicable TEST1-TEST12 suites using each claimed stage compiler; fail stage advancement for an omitted/failing applicable suite and do not infer full-language support from a subset. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test13/trusting-trust: Support release trust with reproducible builds or diverse double compilation where applicable; reject unreproducible releases when policy requires reproducibility. Concrete acceptance: Perform policy-applicable reproducible or diverse double compilation with actual compiler/toolchain identities; fail unexplained output drift, missing diversity where required or a trust claim based only on source language. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. This producer supplies conformance evidence; independent intermediate admission and final release remain separate consumers. Current implementation acceptance is unassessed.",
